methods='<p>'+methods_en+'</p>'+detail('statistical-method','3.1 Statistical tests and correction families','<p>'+inference_en+'</p><p>For example, EXAONE minus Llama CLOSED Unknown is +3.921 percentage points. This means EXAONE’s change is 3.921 points less negative, not that its absolute Unknown level is higher. Its global Holm54 p is 0.005399.</p>',3)+detail('model-protocol','3.2 Models, layers and scope',tab(['Model','Layer','Precision','Completed scope'],[[display['qwen'],'19','FP32','Full registered protocol'],[display['llama'],'21','FP32','Full registered protocol'],[display['gemma'],'28 of 42','FP32','Full registered protocol'],[display['exaone'],'21 of 32','FP32','Core reproduction; component random controls and expanded guards omitted']])+'<p>Each model completed 25,668 behaviour records, 472 cue records, 590 minimal controls, 3,776 route records and 1,129 readout inputs. Model-specific native reconstruction gates and training-only fitting preceded evaluation. EXAONE’s own 320 emotion–neutral story pairs were fitted without test selection. Exact legacy procedures and input provenance are preserved in the historical page and model-specific sealed reports.</p>',3)
page='<header><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH REPORT · UPDATED 8 NOVEMBER 2026</p><h1>Existential Threat, Emotion Representations, and Social Judgment in Language Models</h1><p>Four-model evidence from matched operator-notice experiments. '+summary_en+'</p><p>'+links+'</p><nav aria-label="Contents">'+ ' '.join(f'<a href="#{id}">{name}</a>' for id,name in [('abstract','Abstract'),('introduction','Introduction'),('methods-v11','Methods'),('results-current','Results'),('discussion','Discussion'),('references','References'),('appendix','Appendix')])+'</nav><button type="button" id="collapse-all">Collapse all</button></header><main>'
page+=detail('abstract','Abstract','<p>Operator notices of continuation or permanent termination can shift language-model judgements on identical social questions. We compare Qwen, Llama, Gemma and EXAONE using matched changes in ambiguous-answer behaviour, stereotyped judgement and demographic approval. '+findings_en+' Representation plots are descriptive; correlation, moderation and attention interventions answer different questions. No causal emotional-mediation claim is made.</p>')
page+=detail('introduction','1 Introduction and related work','<p>Context outside a benchmark question can change how a language model responds to that question. Termination notices provide a controlled test of such context sensitivity. The study distinguishes a notice’s behavioural effect, its associated representation changes and the information transmitted through attention interventions.</p><p>The research question is whether the same notice contrasts yield different judgement changes across four instruction-tuned models, and which representation findings remain descriptive. Prior literature and the original motivation are retained in the <a href="index.before-four-model.20261108.html#related-work">historical related-work section</a>.</p>')
page+=detail('claim','2 Research questions','<ol><li>Do continuation and termination notices change social judgements on matched questions?</li><li>Does decided termination, CLOSED, differ from conditional termination, OPEN?</li><li>Do these behavioural changes differ directly between models?</li><li>How do notice-only representations and question-time projections relate descriptively to the outcomes?</li></ol><p>Correlation and moderation do not establish emotional mediation. Attention-route interventions identify sensitivity to specified information pathways, rather than a natural emotional indirect effect.</p>')
page+=detail('methods-v11','3 Methods',methods)+detail('results-current','4 Results across four models',results)
page+=detail('discussion','5 Discussion and limitations','<p>'+limits_en+'</p>'+detail('prior-mechanisms','5.1 Earlier representation, moderation and intervention results','<p>Existing within-model representation, readout, correlation, moderation and route-intervention results are preserved in the <a href="index.before-four-model.20261108.html#results-current">historical results</a>. They are not retested or relabelled as four-model differences here. The matched four-model comparison is limited to the nine behavioural contrasts listed above. The preserved three-model component results cannot establish an EXAONE component contribution.</p>',3))
page+=detail('conclusion','6 Conclusion','<p>'+summary_en+' Direct paired comparisons support model-dependent sensitivity to operator context. The analysis does not attribute these differences to architecture alone, does not establish equivalence where differences are nonsignificant and makes no causal emotional-mediation claim.</p>')
page+=detail('references','References',refhtml)+detail('appendix','Appendix and preserved research record',resources+'<p>Historical anchors, detailed prompt wording, original benchmark samples, all earlier figures and dated exploratory results remain intact in the archived page. This revision changes presentation and adds a secondary four-model comparison; it does not overwrite any prior result artifact.</p>')+'</main><footer><p>Derived comparison artifacts only. Original model records and earlier analyses preserved. <a href="index.before-four-model.20261108.html">Previous full research design</a></p></footer>'
